WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.522
A merge can run successfully and still produce unexpected matches, so join validation matters.

00:00:07.522 --> 00:00:14.082
The orders table contains C101, C102, and C999.

00:00:14.082 --> 00:00:17.932
The customer table contains only C101 and C102.

00:00:17.932 --> 00:00:25.834
A left join keeps every order and attaches customer information where a match exists.

00:00:26.582 --> 00:00:30.914
Indicator equals True creates the _merge column.

00:00:30.914 --> 00:00:38.654
C101 and C102 should be both, while C999 should be left_only.

00:00:38.654 --> 00:00:46.487
That small check makes missing keys visible instead of letting them pass unnoticed.
